---
title: "Geology"
---

## GOL 105 - Physical Geology
**Credits**: 4

Introduces the science of physical geology through a comprehensive systems-based examination of Earth’s structure, composition, rocks and minerals, landforms, geomorphology, and agents responsible for shaping and modifying its environments. Explores the origin and evolution of Earth’s topographic and bathymetric features, geologic phenomena, and geologic hazards, resulting from plate tectonics. Lecture 3 hours. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 6 hours per week.

## GOL 106 - Historical Geology
**Credits**: 4

Traces the evolution of the earth and life through time. Presents scientific theories of the origin of the earth and life and interprets rock and fossil record. Lecture 3 hours, Laboratory 3 hours, Total 6 hours per week.

## GOL 299 - Supervised Study
**Credits**: 1

Assigns problems for independent study incorporating previous instruction and supervised by the instructor.

May be repeated for credit. Variable hours.
